---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/patterns/PageIntro.astro';
import Section from '../components/primitives/Section.astro';
import Prose from '../components/primitives/Prose.astro';
import Button from '../components/primitives/Button.astro';
import NowBand from '../components/patterns/NowBand.astro';
import ProjectEntry from '../components/patterns/ProjectEntry.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
import { publishedProjects } from '../utils/projects';

const projects = publishedProjects(await getCollection('projects'));
const now = (await getCollection('now'))[0]?.data;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Om Jhamvar — how I work, what I am building, and the long-term record this site is for."
  jsonLd="BreadcrumbList"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', item: site.url },
    { name: 'About', item: `${site.url}/about` },
  ]}
>
  <main id="main">
    <div class="container">
      <PageIntro
        kicker="The person"
        title="About me"
        lede="I am Om Jhamvar, an 11th grade student in Mumbai. I learn best by building things, writing about them, and doing both in public."
      />
    </div>

    <Section kicker="How I work" heading="Make it real, then explain it" id="how-i-work" headingLevel="h2">
      <Prose>
        <p>
          I started this site so learning would have somewhere to go. Instead of stopping at a
          tutorial or a class, I try to turn what I am studying into something I can point at — a
          project, a system, or a piece of writing that will not let me stay vague.
        </p>
        <p>
          That is also how I check whether I understood anything. If I cannot explain what I built
          and why a decision survived contact with execution — where it broke, what it cost to
          fix, what I would do the second time — I did not understand it yet.
        </p>
        <p>
          A lot of that habit comes from watching sport as a system, not a highlight reel.
          Football, Formula 1, tennis, cricket, and the NFL are hours of tactics, decisions under
          pressure, and patterns over a season. I read code the same way.
        </p>
        <p>
          Music is the long thread. I play guitar and piano, sing, and have performed at school
          concerts. LCM Grade 8 Guitar with High Distinction took years of graded exams; I am
          working toward the diploma. Daily practice is where I learned what patience actually
          costs, which is a more useful lesson than it sounds.
        </p>
        <p>
          A month at Ashoka University on the Lodha Genius Programme was the first time my days
          were mostly mine to structure. The useful part was not the brochure — it was noticing
          that independence is a set of small choices, not a personality trait. I wrote that up
          in{' '}
          <a
            class="link-external"
            href="https://blog.beyondthebasics.me/article/my-summer-at-ashoka-university"
            rel="noopener"
          >
            My Summer at Ashoka University
          </a>.
        </p>
      </Prose>
    </Section>

    {
      now && (
        <Section kicker="Currently" heading="What has my attention" id="now" headingLevel="h2">
          <NowBand entry={now} />
        </Section>
      )
    }

    <Section kicker="What I build" heading="Tools I wish I had" id="build" headingLevel="h2">
      <Prose>
        <p>
          The work on this site is narrow on purpose: software that gives a learner more useful
          practice than a classroom minute allows, and hardware when I need to understand a system
          in the physical world. Two projects are published so far.
        </p>
      </Prose>
      {
        projects.length > 0 && (
          <div class="stack">
            {projects.map((project) => (
              <ProjectEntry
                project={project}
                variant="compact"
                href={`/projects/${project.id}`}
              />
            ))}
          </div>
        )
      }
      <p class="band-action">
        <Button href="/projects" variant="quiet" size="md">All projects →</Button>
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section kicker="Direction" heading="A record, not a pitch" id="direction" headingLevel="h2">
      <Prose>
        <p>
          I am not using this site as a campaign. I am trying to keep an honest public record of
          how I think and what I can actually do — the projects, the writing, and the few
          credentials that have an issuing body. If that is useful to someone else later, good.
          The first reader is me in six months.
        </p>
      </Prose>
      <p class="band-action">
        <Button href="/achievements" variant="quiet" size="md">Achievements →</Button>
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section kicker="Contact" heading="If you want to talk" id="connect" headingLevel="h2">
      <p class="band-text">
        A question about a project, a collaboration, or an argument about football tactics — the
        contact page is the right door. I reply within a day or so.
      </p>
      <p class="band-action">
        <Button href="/contact" variant="primary">Get in touch</Button>
      </p>
    </Section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .band-text {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: var(--measure-prose);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .band-action {
    margin: var(--space-5) 0 0;
  }
</style>
